--- !u!114 &691527665
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 691527660}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2d40465983d6ad949b1b9d4a3d48f83f, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InterrogationManager
  suspects:
  - displayName: Warren Batey
    background: {fileID: 0}
    portraitNeutral: {fileID: 0}
    portraitOnCorrect: {fileID: 0}
    portraitOnWrong: {fileID: 0}
    rounds:
    - promptVariations:
      - You say you were in the shed. Whose shoes left these by the grave?
      - Somebody washed a rock from your border pile. Know anything about it?
      - The side gate was set for a midnight visitor. Did you lock up?
      choices:
      - itemName: You did nothing.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: You stayed inside.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: You left the house.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 1
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      correctReactions:
      - Hanno glances at his own polished heels before he can stop himself. "Half the house wears shoes like these." He says it a beat too fast.
      - His eyes drop to his coat hem, then back up. "Gray wool is hardly rare, detective." His hand drifts to cover a small tear.
      - '"A routine pickup. Appraisers arrange these things." He never explains why it was set for midnight.'
      wrongReactions:
      - '"I fail to see the relevance." He smooths his cuff and gives a thin, patient smile.'
      - '"A scrap of nothing. I''ve been indoors all night." He sounds almost bored.'
      - '"You are fishing, and not very well." He folds his hands and waits.'
    - promptVariations:
      - You thought Aldous was letting you go. Read this.
      - Whoever was out there wore these. Are they yours?
      - Someone certified this vase. Can you read it?
      choices:
      - itemName: You wanted his estate.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: You forged the pieces.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 1
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: You owed him money.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      correctReactions:
      - '"That is my work, yes. Everything I certify is in order." His voice stays level, but he never asks where you found it.'
      - Hanno goes still. "An old man's notes. He doubted everything lately." For the first time, he won't meet your eyes.
      - '"Cleaning gloves. We all use them." He tucks his own hands into his pockets, an odd move for a man who gestures constantly.'
      wrongReactions:
      - '"Aldous valued my opinion above anyone''s." He looks almost wounded.'
      - '"He was sharp, but he trusted me completely." He steeples his fingers. "You are wasting your time."'
      - '"A glove, how fascinating. Perhaps one of the staff left it." He shrugs.'
    - promptVariations:
      - Did you see anyone wearing something like this tonight?
      - Aldous held this when he died. Who carries paper like it?
      - These narrow prints crossed the grave. Did you see their owner?
      choices:
      - itemName: You struck him down.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 1
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: It was self-defense.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: Warren did it.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      correctReactions:
      - '"I don''t handle rocks." He swallows. A faint smudge of the same white dust shows on his cuff.'
      - Hanno stares at the half seal and the color leaves his face. "That could be anyone's paper," he says, but his voice cracks on the last word.
      - He hesitates too long. The torn hem matches the scrap. "You have no idea what he threatened to do to me," he says, which is not a denial.
      wrongReactions:
      - '"Rocks, gloves, scraps. This is a pile of rubbish, not a case." He is composed again.'
      - '"A scrap of paper. I fail to see how it concerns me." He checks his watch.'
      - '"Search it all you like. You will find a coat." He hands it over with a smirk.'
  - displayName: Hanno Leclair
    background: {fileID: 0}
    portraitNeutral: {fileID: 0}
    portraitOnCorrect: {fileID: 0}
    portraitOnWrong: {fileID: 0}
    rounds:
    - promptVariations:
      - You say you never left the house. Do your shoes agree?
      - Someone was at the old pillar around midnight. Look at this.
      - Your side gate had a visitor scheduled for midnight. Care to explain?
      choices:
      - itemName: You left the house.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 1
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: You stayed inside.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: Pryce was outside.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      correctReactions:
      - Hanno glances at his own polished heels before he can stop himself. "Half the house wears shoes like these." He says it a beat too fast.
      - His eyes drop to his coat hem, then back up. "Gray wool is hardly rare, detective." His hand drifts to cover a small tear.
      - '"A routine pickup. Appraisers arrange these things." He never explains why it was set for midnight.'
      wrongReactions:
      - '"I fail to see the relevance." He smooths his cuff and gives a thin, patient smile.'
      - '"A scrap of nothing. I''ve been indoors all night." He sounds almost bored.'
      - '"You are fishing, and not very well." He folds his hands and waits.'
    - promptVariations:
      - Mr. Thorne trusted your signature. Does this look familiar?
      - Aldous was going over his collection. What do you think he found?
      - Someone has been aging new pieces. Whose hands do you think these are?
      choices:
      - itemName: You owed him money.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: You wanted his estate.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: You forged the pieces.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 1
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      correctReactions:
      - '"That is my work, yes. Everything I certify is in order." His voice stays level, but he never asks where you found it.'
      - Hanno goes still. "An old man's notes. He doubted everything lately." For the first time, he won't meet your eyes.
      - '"Cleaning gloves. We all use them." He tucks his own hands into his pockets, an odd move for a man who gestures constantly.'
      wrongReactions:
      - '"Aldous valued my opinion above anyone''s." He looks almost wounded.'
      - '"He was sharp, but he trusted me completely." He steeples his fingers. "You are wasting your time."'
      - '"A glove, how fascinating. Perhaps one of the staff left it." He shrugs.'
    - promptVariations:
      - A rock from the pile was cleaned and used. Look closer.
      - Aldous died holding something. Do you recognize it?
      - Take off your coat, Mr. Leclair. Let's see how it fits this.
      choices:
      - itemName: Warren did it.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: You struck him down.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 1
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: It was self-defense.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      correctReactions:
      - '"I don''t handle rocks." He swallows. A faint smudge of the same white dust shows on his cuff.'
      - Hanno stares at the half seal and the color leaves his face. "That could be anyone's paper," he says, but his voice cracks on the last word.
      - He hesitates too long. The torn hem matches the scrap. "You have no idea what he threatened to do to me," he says, which is not a denial.
      wrongReactions:
      - '"Rocks, gloves, scraps. This is a pile of rubbish, not a case." He is composed again.'
      - '"A scrap of paper. I fail to see how it concerns me." He checks his watch.'
      - '"Search it all you like. You will find a coat." He hands it over with a smirk.'
  - displayName: Pryce Vane
    background: {fileID: 0}
    portraitNeutral: {fileID: 0}
    portraitOnCorrect: {fileID: 0}
    portraitOnWrong: {fileID: 0}
    rounds:
    - promptVariations:
      - Your uncle left a note about a midnight meeting. Did you know?
      - A set of narrow heel prints crossed the garden. Are they yours?
      - Someone cleaned a rock in the garden. Where were you at midnight?
      choices:
      - itemName: Pour me one.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: You're free to go.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: Drop the act.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 1
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      correctReactions:
      - Pryce reads it and pales. "Midnight at the pillar? I swear I didn't know. I was in the library, drinking my own bad decisions."
      - The grin fades. He lifts a foot. "Mine are blunter. I've never owned shoes that narrow, and my tailor has tried."
      - He sets the glass down. "Library, until I gave up and went to bed. The garden gives me hives."
      wrongReactions:
      - '"Uncle never told me anything, that was the problem." He laughs a little too loudly.'
      - '"Do I look like a man who goes mud walking?" He waves a hand. "Come on."'
      - '"Rocks? You''re grasping." He tries a grin that doesn''t land'
    - promptVariations:
      - You inherit the estate. Did you know pieces were being shipped out?
      - You inherit the estate. Did your uncle ever doubt his pieces?
      - Plenty will say you did this for the money. Whose gloves are these?
      choices:
      - itemName: Who else benefits?
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 1
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: You needed money.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: You hated him.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      correctReactions:
      - '"Not me, and I''d love the money." He reads the slip twice. "That''s not our usual carrier. Somebody was selling quietly."'
      - '"He said something at dinner about copies and raised his voice at someone." Pryce rubs his neck. "I assumed it was the appraiser."'
      - He wrinkles his nose. "It stinks of tea and ash. I own gloves that cost more than this barrel, and none are brown. Who handles that mess?"
      wrongReactions:
      - '"Shipping? I can barely manage my own luggage." He chuckles. "Next question."'
      - '"I only care about the vases with cash in them." He smirks, then stops when he sees your face.'
      - '"I only care about the vases with cash in them." He smirks, then stops when he sees your face.'
    - promptVariations:
      - Aldous held this when he died. Seen it before?
      - Did you see anyone wearing gray tonight?
      - The chest was opened without force. You have a key, don't you?
      choices:
      - itemName: Nothing, then.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: Case closed.
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 0
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      - itemName: What are you hiding?
        variants: []
        isCorrect: 1
        pointsOverride: 0
        reaction: []
      correctReactions:
      - '"That''s the appraiser''s good stock. He stamped it on everything. I saw him hand a sheet to my uncle at dinner."'
      - '"The appraiser wore a gray coat at dinner. He had a row with Uncle over the soup." He winces. "I should have said sooner."'
      - Pryce sinks into a chair. "Fine. I took some cash around ten, with a spare key. I saw the 'copy' marks, panicked, and left. I'm not proud of it."
      wrongReactions:
      - '"Paper. He kept a lot of it." Pryce shrugs, bad at hiding his nerves.'
      - '"Gray? Half the guests wore gray." He tugs at his collar.'
      - '"I have no idea what you mean." He laughs, but the laugh slips.'
